One line per native function that ran from plugin load to the end of the run, most frequent first.
queued = run from the queue by a stock update, extra = run from the queue by an extra cycle, direct = called directly by a tasklet, other = any other path or a frame the hooks did not collect in (loading, the 10 s hold after a load, catch-up not engaged).
name_rule = the release judgement, without_pt_list = the same without the Papyrus Tweaks exclusion list, reviewed = the read list of that build, which held only the helper natives (Math, StringUtil, Debug.Trace/TraceStack).
Totals in collected frames: queued 12831, extra 3207, direct 25484. Read by name: 164 natives (queued 9315, extra 2697, direct 10484). Held only by the Papyrus Tweaks list: 16 natives (queued 1201, extra 38, direct 20).
The 52-entry measurement list of the 15:21 build (IsListedReadNative) covers 92.1% of the calls of read-named non-helper natives and 96.5% of their queued calls.

CORRECTION (2026-11-10 16:21): the 1966 lines below are NOT 1966 different natives. This run keyed the counts by function-object address, and the getter/setter objects of auto properties (which also report GetIsNative) are created and released again, so one property appears on many lines and a reused address can add one property's calls to another's line. There are 630 distinct class.name pairs: 589 native functions and 41 auto properties (1377 lines, 5724 direct calls, all judged change). The totals per rule above and the coverage figures are unaffected, because every duplicated line is an auto property and none of them is read-named; the per-property counts are unreliable. Builds from 16:21 on key the census by class and name and mark auto properties with kind=property.
